<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M2, AC2.5 / D3a: an ORDINARY edit invalidates THROUGH an empty
  master chain.

  THIS IS THE COMMONEST PATH IN THE APP AND IT IS SILENT WHEN WRONG. Every
  user has an empty master chain and edits clips. After M2 put the master
  lane's twPluginChain and twGainStage between the bus sum and the rewire,
  each carries its own page cache and neither was bumped by anybody on an
  ordinary edit: SStdMixer::bumpRenderChainEpoch() knew about the bus mixers
  and the rewire and nothing in between. The rewire re-freezes, fetchInputPage
  serves the gain stage's still-valid stale page, and THE EDIT IS INAUDIBLE -
  no error, no log line, just the old audio.

  It is a DIFFERENT edge from D11's "invalidation FROM the master", which
  master_insert_heard.qxa gates, and neither subsumes the other: this one
  carries an ordinary TRACK edit past the master, that one carries a MASTER
  edit down to the rewire. Reverting either leaves the other green.

  MEASURED, NOT PREDICTED: with the wiring in and the epoch extension missing,
  mc_golden_stereo's own negative control flipped - its set-track-mute plus
  re-render produced a file BYTE-IDENTICAL to the unmuted golden, so the
  assertion that exists to prove the comparison CAN fail reported "applied but
  expectReject was set". A mute had stopped being audible.

  Closed form over ../test_autosaw.wav as in master_fader_heard.qxa: base
  0.230956 over [48000, 96000) channel 0; at -6.0 dB, 0.115747.

  THE MASTER CHAIN IS EMPTY THROUGHOUT, deliberately. An insert on the master
  would give the edit a second way to reach the rewire and would stop this
  case from being about the empty-chain path every user actually has.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="track_edit_invalidates_through_master">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="0" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <assert-system-lane trackPath="$master" role="master" plugins="0" volume="0.0"/>

    <!-- Freeze the pages first. Without this render there is nothing stale to
         serve and the case cannot fail. -->
    <render filename="teim_base.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="teim_base.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.2300" maxRms="0.2320"/>

    <!-- (1) A TRACK fader edit, in the same process, must reach the render
             through the master's empty chain and gain stage. -->
    <set-track-volume trackPath="0" volume="-6.0"/>
    <render filename="teim_fader.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="teim_fader.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.1152" maxRms="0.1163"/>

    <!-- (2) A CLIP edit, which travels the range-scoped path
             (bumpRenderChainEpochRange) rather than the whole-chain one. The
             two are separate functions and were separately blind, so one
             assertion cannot stand for both: muting the clip's track silences
             the window entirely. -->
    <set-track-volume trackPath="0" volume="0.0"/>
    <set-track-mute trackPath="0" muted="1"/>
    <render filename="teim_muted.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="teim_muted.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.0005"/>

    <!-- ...and back to exactly the base. -->
    <set-track-mute trackPath="0" muted="0"/>
    <render filename="teim_back.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-file-identical actual="teim_back.wav" expected="teim_base.wav"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
